  "Question": "In July \\(1861,\\) \\(366\\) inches of rain fell in Cherrapunji, India. What was the average rainfall in inches per hour during that month?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(\\dfrac{366}{31 \\times 24}\\)",
    "B": "\\(\\dfrac{366 \\times 31}{24}\\)",
    "C": "\\(\\dfrac{366 \\times 24}{31}\\)",
    "D": "\\(\\dfrac{31 \\times 24}{366}\\)",
    "E": "\\(366 \\times 31 \\times 24\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Solution": "Average rainfall per hour is the total rainfall divided by the number of hours. July has \\(31\\) days, with \\(24\\) hours in each day, so the month contains \\(31\\times24=744\\) hours. Therefore the average rainfall was\n\\[\n\\frac{366}{31\\times24}\n\\]\ninches per hour, choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{A}}\\).",
